      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "IN THE SUMMERTIME NZ (6) put the writing on the wall when edged out narrowly two back then came from this barrier and raced wide early before pushing to the front and going on to score here last time, getting home by 8.7 metres. At peak fitness now so could take this next step. BELIEVE IN DREAMS (10) worked from this barrier but stuck on well for second at his latest appearance here, beaten 2.4 metres. That was his best result since back-to-back wins in July, one of them coming at this circuit and distance. Big chance. OUR ULTIMATE JANE (9) came from wider on this row and worked but stuck on for a respectable second at her most recent appearance at Leeton. Draws for a nice trail this time and won her lone attempt at this circuit and distance. KIRPHILBRI (5) draws wider but there was merit in last week's effort for second at Leeton.",
